WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:02.787
Imagine the space underneath the car.

2
00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:08.337
If powerful fans remove air from that space, and the edges are sealed, the pressure

3
00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:13.937
beneath the body falls. The surrounding atmosphere now exerts a greater force from

4
00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:18.412
outside. The difference presses the car toward the surface.

5
00:00:18.512 --> 00:00:20.075
This is not free flight.

6
00:00:20.635 --> 00:00:24.260
It is controlled adhesion to a nearby surface.

7
00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:29.675
And it can create levels of grip conventional sports cars cannot reach.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.534
Atmospheric pressure acts on every exposed surface.

9
00:00:33.944 --> 00:00:39.794
If a fan lowers pressure under a nearly sealed floor, outside air pushes down more

10
00:00:39.869 --> 00:00:43.494
strongly than the reduced pressure below pushes up.

11
00:00:43.569 --> 00:00:48.444
The additional normal load is approximately pressure difference multiplied by

12
00:00:48.494 --> 00:00:49.593
effective area.

13
00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:55.521
That is why a suction car can develop traction even without high road speed.

14
00:00:55.801 --> 00:01:01.276
A fan cannot maintain a useful low-pressure region if outside air simply rushes

15
00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:07.891
underneath. A skirt reduces leakage, but it must accommodate bumps, ground clearance

16
00:01:07.941 --> 00:01:08.713
and steering.

17
00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:15.231
Real systems lose energy through ducting, turbulence, fan inefficiency and sealing

18
00:01:15.281 --> 00:01:20.656
imperfections. Our pressure equation is an educational starting point.

19
00:01:20.731 --> 00:01:26.416
The result is force toward the nearby ground, not force that lifts the car away from

20
00:01:26.466 --> 00:01:26.632
it.

21
00:01:27.013 --> 00:01:32.013
The extra tire loading may permit stronger braking and cornering, but if the road

22
00:01:32.088 --> 00:01:38.463
surface changes or a skirt loses contact, that load can change suddenly.

23
00:01:38.563 --> 00:01:42.716
This is an adhesion system, not sustained flight propulsion.
